You fight the incentive to run away immediately, but it looks like there is nothing to fear. It's clear that the natives feel a mix of adoration, fear, and admiration toward you. In their opinion, you are true gods restoring their fire. And, in principle, you almost didn't lie to them. Well, maybe a little bit.

Doyle grew bolder and speaks to the chief about something, then turns to you and says, "The entire tribe thanks us. I told them that we came from the Gods' Island. The chief knows how to get to the shore and promised to provide us with his best warriors. They will accompany us."